            <div xml:id="d436">

                <pb facs="0380" n="368" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg368"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.7962/61: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wharton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-13T16:00:00-04:00">March 13, 1942—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>52. Your 71, March 12, 3 p.m.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d436-f1"/> For McBride from
                    Villard. Text of agreement is satisfactory as far as we are concerned but War
                    Department has not yet given its approval. Except for possible minor
                    modifications we do not believe that any change will be necessary. Official
                    reply will be sent as soon as possible.</p>
                <p>Please repeat last paragraph of Legation’s 68, March 11, 9 a.m., which appears
                    incomplete. Our telegram regarding Lend-Lease aid should more than answer credit
                    question.</p>
                <p>Congratulations on excellent work so far. [Villard.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
